NAME
     tail - the last part of a file

SYNOPSIS
     tail [-n LINES] [-c BYTES] [-f] [FILE...]

DESCRIPTION
     tail copies the last ten lines of each FILE, or of standard input.

OPTIONS
     -n LINES   how many lines; +N means from line N onwards
     -c BYTES   that many bytes instead of lines
     -f         keep watching, and print what is added

SEE ALSO
     head(1), less(1)
